Z||000006||hugh||04-03-2001||06:44 PM||||I have a rear engine dragster that I have had certified a couple of times.They only check the structure of the drivers compartment.They check for placement of all the required braces,their diameter and the metal thickness of all the tubing.They are as thorough as can be technically possible.The rest of the machine is left to the tech crew when they inspect your car.There have been some tremendous accidents involving vehicles going in excess of 250 mph with only minor injuries,thanks to the NHRA concentration on safety.||||reg||1
